The market price of our common stock may be volatile, and you could lose all or part of your investment.

The trading price of our common stock is likely to be volatile. The stock market recently has experienced extreme volatility. This volatility often has been unrelated or disproportionate to the operating performance of particular companies. You may not be able to resell your shares of common stock and/or public warrants at an attractive price due to a number of factors such as those listed in this Risk Factors section and the following:

